**Theorem 5.2 (Exact all-history mixed-port error).** The port (5.2) is
legal, with twenty-seven nonzero rank-one composite Kraus matrices
and full input marginal $I_5/5$. With $a,b,c$ from (2.8), define

$$
\begin{gathered}
a_p=(1-p)a+p/2,\qquad b_p=(1-p)b,\qquad c_p=(1-p)c-p/6,\\
C_p=\begin{pmatrix}a_p&b_p\\b_p&c_p\end{pmatrix},\qquad
q_p(z)=z^2-(a_p+c_p)z+a_pc_p-b_p^2,\\
\lambda_{\rm mix}=
\frac{a_p+c_p+\sqrt{(a_p-c_p)^2+4b_p^2}}2.
\end{gathered}
\tag{5.3}
$$

The nonnegative radical specifies the unique positive root of $q_p$.
Then, for every complex density input and every actual finite adaptive
history,

$$
e(T_{\rm mix})=\lambda_{\rm mix},\qquad
\frac{52417598}{10^8}<\lambda_{\rm mix}<\frac{52417600}{10^8}
<\lambda_{\delta_*}<\lambda_Q.
\tag{5.4}
$$

Only $N$ attains the fifteen-event maximum. A pure input, actual
wait zero, one complete five-outcome read and Stop attain this error.

Proof. The two encoder families each sum to $I$ before their outer
scaling. Thus the full encoder sum is $(1-p)I+pI=I$.
Every decoder column $Da_f$ has norm one, so it is TP on all of
$M_1$, and each composite $\sqrt{w_f}Da_fb_f^TD^\dagger$ is nonzero
of rank one. The sandwich proof gives CP at every reference dimension.
No original input or mixture flag is supplied to the future policy.
The output-first normalized Choi state has marginal $I_5/5$;
all three marginal equations are retained. The channel is stationary
and reflected because both summands are so on all complex matrices.

Every residual uses the actual adjoint of this one channel:

$$
H_J(S_{\rm mix})=(1-p)H_J(S_Q)+pH_J(\mathcal B).
\tag{5.5}
$$

Formula (2.5) at $\delta=0$ and formula (3.3) specify all fifteen
